   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 267 of the laws of 1988, amending the parks, recreation and historic preservation law relating to the lease of state property included in the Glimmerglass state park, in relation to extending the expiration and repeal of the provisions thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S7490",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7490-2015",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2, Chap 267 of 1988",
    "lawSection": "Parks",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S7490\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend chapter 267 of the laws of 1988,\namending the parks, recreation and historic preservation law relating\nto the lease of state property included in the Glimmerglass state\npark, in relation to extending the expiration and repeal of the\nprovisions thereof\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nTo extend chapter 267 of the laws of 1988 for an additional thirty\n(30) years beyond its current expiration date of January 1, 2017\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection one outlines the purpose of amending, and does amend, section\n2 of chapter 267 of the laws of 1988. Section two provides for a\nrevised expiration date of January 1, 2047.\n\nSection three provides the new effective date of the bill.\n\n EXISTING LAW :\n\nChapter 267 of the laws of 1988 expire on January 1, 2017.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThe state Office of Parks, Recreation and Historic Preservation (OPR)\nhas enjoyed a beneficial relationship with the Friends of Hyde Hall, a\nnonprofit organization dedicated to the preservation and public\nenjoyment of Hyde Hall, a historic estate located on the grounds of\nthe Glimmerglass State Park. Friends of Hyde Hall operates the\nhistoric site at Hyde Hall and has raised funds to restore the hall to\nits historic and original condition, making the site open to the\npublic for cultural programs, visits, tours, and public events.\nExtension of the lease, so that the Friends of Hyde Hall can continue\nto operate and raise funds for this state historic treasure, is the\nperfect example of a state-private partnership and is in the interests\nof the state of New York, our history, and our heritage.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew bill\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone to the state. The partnership has raised tens of thousands of\nprivate dollars that have improved, preserved and protected this state\nhistoric site.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediate\n",
